IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja1-part2-hearings`

-- Tests for scja1-part2-hearings.l4 (ss 8, 8A). Expected values are written from the text (SCJA1969.txt lines 521-751), not from the code.

§ `Fixtures`

`a no-judges bench of the General Division` MEANS Bench OF `General Division`, EMPTY
`no split of opinion` MEANS `Split of opinion` OF 0, 0

GIVEN manner IS A `Manner of hearing`
      nature IS A `Nature of the proceeding`
      oral IS A BOOLEAN
      consent IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Hearing
`a hearing` MEANS Hearing OF `a no-judges bench of the General Division`, manner, nature, oral, consent, FALSE, `no split of opinion`

§§ `s 8(1): the place of the court is open and public`

#ASSERT (`s 8(1) the place is deemed an open and public court to which the public generally may have access` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(1) the place is deemed an open and public court to which the public generally may have access` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 8(2): sitting in private`

#ASSERT (`s 8(2) the court has power to hear the matter or proceeding in private` (LIST `s 8(2) the interests of justice`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(2) the court has power to hear the matter or proceeding in private` (LIST `s 8(2) public safety`, `s 8(2) propriety`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(2) the court has power to hear the matter or proceeding in private` (LIST `s 8(2) other sufficient reason`)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "if the court is satisfied": no ground the court is satisfied of, no power.
#ASSERT (`s 8(2) the court has power to hear the matter or proceeding in private` EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 8(2AA), (2AB): national interest and national security applications`

#ASSERT (`s 8(2AA) the application is to be heard in private` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(2AA) the application is to be heard in private` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2AB): both (a) and (b) must be satisfied.
#ASSERT (`s 8(2AB) the court has power to hear the application otherwise than in private` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(2AB) the court has power to hear the application otherwise than in private` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 8(2AB) the court has power to hear the application otherwise than in private` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 8(2AB) the court has power to hear the application otherwise than in private` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Together: heard in private unless the court has the (2AB) power; with the power, the Act does not say whether it is used.
#ASSERT (`ss 8(2AA) and 8(2AB) the application will be heard in private` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`ss 8(2AA) and 8(2AB) the application will be heard in private` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`ss 8(2AA) and 8(2AB) the application will be heard in private` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`ss 8(2AA) and 8(2AB) the application will be heard in private` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 8(2A): removal or redaction in a court document`

#ASSERT (`s 8(2A) the court has power to order the thing removed or sufficiently redacted` `s 8(2A)(a) the name, address or photograph of a witness` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(2A) the court has power to order the thing removed or sufficiently redacted` `s 8(2A)(b) evidence or another thing likely to lead to the identification of such a witness by a person other than a party` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(2A) the court has power to order the thing removed or sufficiently redacted` `s 8(2A)(c) information that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not satisfied that it is expedient: the "if" fails, no.
#ASSERT (`s 8(2A) the court has power to order the thing removed or sufficiently redacted` `s 8(2A)(a) the name, address or photograph of a witness` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not in a court document intended to be produced before the court, or not one of (a) to (c): the section does not speak of it.
#ASSERT (`s 8(2A) the court has power to order the thing removed or sufficiently redacted` `s 8(2A)(a) the name, address or photograph of a witness` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 8(2A) the court has power to order the thing removed or sufficiently redacted` `s 8(2A) another thing` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 8(3), (4): orders that no person is to publish or identify, and the offence`

#ASSERT (`s 8(3) the court may order that no person is to do the act` `s 8(3)(a) publishing the name, address or photograph of a witness, or evidence or another thing likely to lead to the identification of such a witness`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(3) the court may order that no person is to do the act` `s 8(3)(b) doing another act likely to lead to the identification of such a witness`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(3) the court may order that no person is to do the act` `s 8(3)(c) publishing information relating to the matter that, if disclosed, may be prejudicial to the national interest or national security of Singapore`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(3) the court may order that no person is to do the act` `s 8(3) another act`) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`s 8(4) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(4) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the highest fine` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `s 8(4) the longest imprisonment, in years` EQUALS 3
-- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both"
#ASSERT (`s 8(4) the sentence is within what the person is liable to on conviction` 5000 0) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(4) the sentence is within what the person is liable to on conviction` 0 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(4) the sentence is within what the person is liable to on conviction` 5000 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(4) the sentence is within what the person is liable to on conviction` 0 0) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(4) the sentence is within what the person is liable to on conviction` 5001 0) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 8(4) the sentence is within what the person is liable to on conviction` 0 4) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 8(5), (6), (7): who may be present, and what the court may consider`

#ASSERT (`s 8(5) the court may permit the individual to be present in the courtroom` `s 8(5)(a) a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(5) the court may permit the individual to be present in the courtroom` `s 8(5)(b) an individual the court determines has a sufficient interest in the matter or proceeding` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(5) the court may permit the individual to be present in the courtroom` `s 8(5)(c) any other individual that the court specifies in the particular case` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A court that does not hear the matter in private: the provision does not speak of it.
#ASSERT (`s 8(5) the court may permit the individual to be present in the courtroom` `s 8(5)(a) a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 8(5) the court may permit the individual to be present in the courtroom` `s 8(5) another individual` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`s 8(6) the court may consider the matter in deciding whether to hear in private` `s 8(6)(a) whether the defence of an accused person will be prejudiced by the presence of a member of the public in the courtroom`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(6) the court may consider the matter in deciding whether to hear in private` `s 8(6)(b) whether an accused person or witness has a legitimate interest in privacy that needs to be protected`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(6) the court may consider the matter in deciding whether to hear in private` `s 8(6)(c) whether the object of the matter or proceeding will be defeated by publicity if it is heard in open court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(6) the court may consider the matter in deciding whether to hear in private` `s 8(6)(d) whether an accused person or witness has a legitimate interest in protecting the confidentiality of information that may be disclosed`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(6) the court may consider the matter in deciding whether to hear in private` `s 8(6)(e) whether information that may be disclosed will be prejudicial to the interests of Singapore`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "include": not a closed list.
#ASSERT (`s 8(6) the court may consider the matter in deciding whether to hear in private` `s 8(6) another matter`) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`s 8(7) broadcasting service: it has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Broadcasting Act 1994` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(7) broadcasting service: it has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Broadcasting Act 1994` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 8(7) newspaper: it has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(7) newspaper: it has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 8(5)(a): a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service.
#ASSERT (`s 8(5)(a) the individual is a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(5)(a) the individual is a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8(5)(a) the individual is a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 8(5)(a) the individual is a journalist who reports news for a newspaper or a broadcasting service` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 8A(1), (2): hearing through electronic means`

#ASSERT (`s 8A(1) the court may conduct the hearing of the matter through the means` FALSE `through a live video link` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(1) the court may conduct the hearing of the matter through the means` FALSE `through a live television link` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(1) the court may conduct the hearing of the matter through the means` FALSE `through a live audio link only` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(1) the court may conduct the hearing of the matter through the means` FALSE `in open court` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (other than a matter prescribed by the Rules): excluded in the text's own words.
#ASSERT (`s 8A(1) the court may conduct the hearing of the matter through the means` TRUE `through a live video link` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A way of hearing that is not an electronic means, and not approved: the section does not speak of it.
#ASSERT (`s 8A(1) the court may conduct the hearing of the matter through the means` FALSE `in open court` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 8A(1) the court may conduct the hearing of the matter through the means` FALSE `asynchronously, by exchange of written correspondence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`s 8A(2) section 8A(1) affects the operation of the provision` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(2) section 8A(1) affects the operation of the provision` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 8A(3): no audio-link-only hearing in three cases`

-- (a) criminal proceeding, oral evidence: prohibited.
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3) the court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a criminal proceeding` TRUE FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) with no oral evidence in that part: not within (a); none of the other limbs: no.
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3) the court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a criminal proceeding` FALSE FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) civil proceeding, oral evidence, parties do not all consent: prohibited.
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3) the court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a civil proceeding` TRUE FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b) unless all the parties consent: not prohibited under (b).
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3) the court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a civil proceeding` TRUE TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) no oral evidence: not prohibited under (b).
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3) the court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a civil proceeding` FALSE FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) the matter is prescribed by the Rules: prohibited whatever the evidence.
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3) the court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a civil proceeding` FALSE TRUE) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A hearing with a video link is outside the prohibition's words.
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3) the court must not conduct this part of the hearing through a live audio link only` (`a hearing` `through a live video link` `a criminal proceeding` TRUE FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3)(a) a criminal proceeding where oral evidence is given` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a criminal proceeding` TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3)(a) a criminal proceeding where oral evidence is given` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a civil proceeding` TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3)(b) a civil proceeding where oral evidence is given and the parties do not all consent` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a civil proceeding` TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(3)(b) a civil proceeding where oral evidence is given and the parties do not all consent` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a criminal proceeding` TRUE FALSE)) EQUALS FALSE

-- The same prohibition as a regulative rule, run: where it applies, conducting the part through an audio link only is a breach; where it does not, the rule is FULFILLED at once.
-- (Read from the output of `l4 run`: the first trace ends BREACH, the second and third FULFILLED. See NOTES.md, "What the main binary does not accept".)
#TRACE `s 8A(3) the court shall not conduct the part through a live audio link only` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a criminal proceeding` TRUE FALSE) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 8A(3) the court` DOES `s 8A(3) conducts the part through a live audio link only` AT 0
#TRACE `s 8A(3) the court shall not conduct the part through a live audio link only` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a criminal proceeding` TRUE FALSE) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 8A(3) the court` DOES `s 8A(3) conducts the part through a live audio link only` AT 5
#TRACE `s 8A(3) the court shall not conduct the part through a live audio link only` (`a hearing` `through a live audio link only` `a civil proceeding` TRUE TRUE) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 8A(3) the court` DOES `s 8A(3) conducts the part through a live audio link only` AT 0

§§ `s 8A(4), (5), (6)`

#ASSERT (`s 8A(4) the court is considered to have conducted the part through a live audio link only` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Any of the three facts missing: the Act does not say.
#ASSERT (`s 8A(4) the court is considered to have conducted the part through a live audio link only` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 8A(4) the court is considered to have conducted the part through a live audio link only` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 8A(4) the court is considered to have conducted the part through a live audio link only` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT (`s 8A(5) the court must not conduct the hearing in the manner provided under section 8A(1)` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(5) the court must not conduct the hearing in the manner provided under section 8A(1)` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- s 8A(6): deemed to be sitting at the appointed place, when the hearing is conducted under s 8A(1).
#ASSERT (`s 8A(6) the court is deemed to be sitting at the appointed place` `General Division` TRUE (JUST TRUE) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(6) the court is deemed to be sitting at the appointed place` `Appellate Division` TRUE NOTHING (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(6) the court is deemed to be sitting at the appointed place` `Court of Appeal` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 8A(6) the court is deemed to be sitting at the appointed place` `Court of Appeal` TRUE NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not conducted under s 8A(1): "when" is not met.
#ASSERT (`s 8A(6) the court is deemed to be sitting at the appointed place` `General Division` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A court the section does not name.
#ASSERT (`s 8A(6) the court is deemed to be sitting at the appointed place` `District Court` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
